OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F363A1787789950
OL,3,CBook of condolence opens for rugby
OL,4,Cleague legend Sir Billy Boston
OL,6,FThe club has also arranged a dedicated
OL,7,Farea for supporters wishing to lay
OL,8,Fflowers, scarves, or other personal
OL,9,Fitems in memory of the legendary Welsh
OL,10,Fwinger.
OL,12,FFans are asked to place tributes in
OL,13,Fthe South East Corner of the Brick
OL,14,FCommunity Stadium bowl, located
OL,15,Fdirectly underneath the Sir Billy
OL,16,FBoston Stand signage.
OL,18,FSir Billy, widely regarded as one of
OL,19,Fthe greatest players ever, enjoyed an
OL,20,Fimpressive career with Wigan after
OL,21,Fsigning for the club in 1953.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G2/6
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'R(,,,,,,,,,
